1
00:00:35,000 --> 00:00:36,040
[This drama is fictional
and bears no resemblance to reality]

2
00:00:36,040 --> 00:00:37,040
[Some scenes feature AI technology]

3
00:00:37,040 --> 00:00:38,222
[All child and animal scenes
followed strict safety guidelines]

4
00:00:38,222 --> 00:00:39,913
[Episode 11]

5
00:00:39,913 --> 00:00:42,166
Ju Yi Jae! Yi Jae!

6
00:00:42,166 --> 00:00:45,326
Why are you taking the blame
for someone else's mistake?

7
00:00:45,326 --> 00:00:46,849
Why should you be the one to leave?

8
00:00:46,849 --> 00:00:48,754
Then who should take the blame?

9
00:00:48,754 --> 00:00:52,478
CEO An, Oh Ha Na, or me,
none of us did anything wrong.

10
00:00:56,228 --> 00:00:58,624
Let's just think about the film, Yi Jae.

11
00:00:58,624 --> 00:01:00,190
We're almost there.

12
00:01:00,190 --> 00:01:02,508
Just think of it as
taking my name off the credits.

13
00:01:02,508 --> 00:01:03,572
Nothing is going to change.

14
00:01:03,572 --> 00:01:06,650
How can nothing change? You won't be there!

15
00:01:06,650 --> 00:01:10,971
- You said we'd see this through together!
- This is exactly how we make it to the end.

16
00:01:10,971 --> 00:01:13,198
Please...

17
00:01:13,198 --> 00:01:18,309
Even if this is where my journey ends,
the movie can't end here.

18
00:01:21,373 --> 00:01:23,303
I don't want to.

19
00:01:23,303 --> 00:01:25,470
I can't accept this.

20
00:01:25,470 --> 00:01:29,684
After everything that happened,
thinking of you kept me going.

21
00:01:29,684 --> 00:01:32,415
I believed you'd come back soon,
and then everything would be okay.

22
00:01:32,415 --> 00:01:33,881
And now you're telling me
you won't even be on set?

23
00:01:33,881 --> 00:01:35,554
I don't want that!

24
00:01:35,554 --> 00:01:37,446
Yi Jae...

25
00:01:37,446 --> 00:01:40,319
You said you'd do everything you could, right?

26
00:01:40,962 --> 00:01:42,928
Now, it's my turn.

27
00:02:23,564 --> 00:02:27,629
Look, they took my ad down.

28
00:02:28,441 --> 00:02:31,055
[Advertising inquiries]

29
00:02:31,055 --> 00:02:33,285
Why are you just standing there?

30
00:02:34,147 --> 00:02:37,064
At least let me lean on you.

31
00:02:43,430 --> 00:02:45,939
I saw you still had that photo.

32
00:02:49,517 --> 00:02:52,049
You couldn't even throw it away.

33
00:02:52,049 --> 00:02:55,307
I make promises I can't even keep.

34
00:03:05,519 --> 00:03:08,310
I know I'm being punished.

35
00:03:10,899 --> 00:03:14,111
Can't you forgive me, just for a little while?

36
00:03:14,111 --> 00:03:16,029
Why should I?

37
00:03:16,029 --> 00:03:18,787
Because I don't want to be a coward anymore.

38
00:04:05,698 --> 00:04:07,522
<i>"Here Comes Yi Jae!"</i>

39
00:04:07,522 --> 00:04:10,190
<i>I've traveled all over this country.</i>

40
00:04:10,190 --> 00:04:11,865
<i>Just trust me!</i>

41
00:04:47,955 --> 00:04:49,835
Comrades! Are you ready?

42
00:04:49,835 --> 00:04:52,209
- Yes, ma'am!
- Yes, ma'am!

43
00:04:52,209 --> 00:04:54,667
But where's the Assistant Director?

44
00:05:00,767 --> 00:05:02,690
You're not leaving without me, are you?

45
00:05:02,690 --> 00:05:05,931
- Seriously...
- Come on, hurry up!

46
00:05:05,931 --> 00:05:08,058
Hey...

47
00:05:08,058 --> 00:05:09,267
- Hey...
- All right, then!

48
00:05:09,267 --> 00:05:10,722
Let's go get Director Woo back!

49
00:05:10,722 --> 00:05:13,550
- Sounds good!
- Let's go!

50
00:05:20,766 --> 00:05:22,789
[Director Removal Request and Approval Form]

51
00:05:24,324 --> 00:05:27,184
[Having reviewed the request, we hereby
approve Director Woo Soo Bin's removal]

52
00:05:39,839 --> 00:05:41,804
[Topline Entertainment, CEO: An Su Hui]

53
00:05:45,106 --> 00:05:46,656
CEO An!

54
00:05:46,656 --> 00:05:49,432
This isn't like you. What's stopping you?

55
00:05:49,432 --> 00:05:51,435
Is that a compliment?

56
00:05:54,062 --> 00:05:56,588
Well, do I seem different to you?

57
00:05:56,588 --> 00:05:58,081
That's not what I meant...

58
00:05:58,081 --> 00:06:00,762
I'm asking why you're hesitating.

59
00:06:00,762 --> 00:06:03,777
You can't be the one to step down, right?

60
00:06:04,467 --> 00:06:05,970
What if I do?

61
00:06:05,970 --> 00:06:08,499
If you step down...

62
00:06:08,499 --> 00:06:11,815
then who's going to fill the funding gap?

63
00:06:11,815 --> 00:06:13,689
You expect us to clean up the mess?

64
00:06:13,689 --> 00:06:19,480
Then this film will end up in limbo
and never even get released.

65
00:06:19,480 --> 00:06:23,735
You need to make the best choice now.

66
00:06:24,343 --> 00:06:28,266
So the best choice is removing Director Woo?

67
00:06:28,266 --> 00:06:30,031
Yes, we have to.

68
00:06:30,031 --> 00:06:35,145
Not just from the film,
but from you and Oh Ha Na as well.

69
00:06:35,145 --> 00:06:38,578
The moment Ian Woo's name
is linked to either of you,

70
00:06:38,578 --> 00:06:43,698
this controversy
is all people will think about.

71
00:06:43,698 --> 00:06:47,065
This is giving me a headache.

72
00:06:48,898 --> 00:06:53,073
Right... it's not like
I need to worry about him too.

73
00:07:00,808 --> 00:07:02,497
CEO An!

74
00:07:03,130 --> 00:07:05,346
CEO An! Wait!

75
00:07:07,477 --> 00:07:09,142
What is this?

76
00:07:10,274 --> 00:07:13,475
- Who let you in?
- I forced my way in!

77
00:07:13,475 --> 00:07:17,563
CEO An, we can't make this film
without Director Woo.

78
00:07:17,563 --> 00:07:18,685
We won't.

79
00:07:18,685 --> 00:07:20,557
We're staying with Director Woo
to the very end!

80
00:07:20,557 --> 00:07:23,556
Goodness. This is like
the old Korean film industry.

81
00:07:23,556 --> 00:07:25,709
Teams like this still exist?

82
00:07:25,709 --> 00:07:29,735
Everyone, what are you going to do
if you all get fired?

83
00:07:29,735 --> 00:07:34,081
If we can't do it together, this means nothing.

84
00:07:34,081 --> 00:07:35,472
CEO An,

85
00:07:35,472 --> 00:07:41,169
everyone on this film
is giving it everything they've got.

86
00:07:41,169 --> 00:07:44,882
Please keep this team together.

87
00:07:46,917 --> 00:07:50,399
So you're asking me to step down
instead of Director Woo?

88
00:07:50,399 --> 00:07:52,612
Director Woo told me this.

89
00:07:52,612 --> 00:07:57,684
"No one was at fault,
so no one should have to take the blame."

90
00:07:57,684 --> 00:08:01,690
Even so, he chose to step aside.

91
00:08:01,690 --> 00:08:03,678
For the sake of this film.

92
00:08:05,193 --> 00:08:09,130
<i>I also want a happy ending</i>

93
00:08:09,793 --> 00:08:12,330
<i>with the person I love.</i>

94
00:08:13,619 --> 00:08:18,504
CEO An, you're not the type
to be swayed by emotional appeals!

95
00:08:18,504 --> 00:08:20,778
You need to think about the losses
right in front of us!

96
00:08:20,778 --> 00:08:22,762
What did you say?

97
00:08:25,501 --> 00:08:27,413
That's rich coming from you!

98
00:08:27,413 --> 00:08:29,734
Do you even know
how many crew members we've already lost?

99
00:08:29,734 --> 00:08:33,575
Come on. What, ten people?

100
00:08:33,575 --> 00:08:36,914
We're dealing with
hundreds of millions of won here. Millions!

101
00:08:36,914 --> 00:08:39,199
And all you can think about is the money?

102
00:08:39,199 --> 00:08:43,944
A film's value isn't measured
by your little numbers game!

103
00:08:43,944 --> 00:08:48,451
This whole industry runs on money.
What value are you talking about?

104
00:08:48,451 --> 00:08:50,043
Dreams.

105
00:08:51,686 --> 00:08:53,161
What?

106
00:08:55,056 --> 00:08:57,432
Our dreams live in these films.

107
00:08:58,543 --> 00:09:01,881
And... passion!

108
00:09:01,881 --> 00:09:05,295
And... the romance of filmmaking!

109
00:09:05,295 --> 00:09:07,343
And loyalty, too!

110
00:09:07,343 --> 00:09:10,989
Isn't that obvious just by looking at us?

111
00:09:10,989 --> 00:09:13,327
Good grief...

112
00:09:19,518 --> 00:09:21,485
CEO An,

113
00:09:21,485 --> 00:09:26,502
I think we've explained
why Director Woo needs to stay.

114
00:09:26,502 --> 00:09:29,157
The people who truly own this set...

115
00:09:29,157 --> 00:09:33,126
are the crew standing here, not the investors.

116
00:09:35,842 --> 00:09:39,621
Please make the right decision.

117
00:09:39,621 --> 00:09:41,503
I'm asking you.

118
00:09:53,999 --> 00:09:55,622
CEO An!

119
00:09:55,622 --> 00:09:57,264
I'll think about it.

120
00:09:57,264 --> 00:10:01,351
- Thank you!
- Thank you so much!

121
00:10:01,351 --> 00:10:03,493
CEO An! You can't do this!

122
00:10:03,493 --> 00:10:07,844
- It has to be approved today.
- I said I need more time!

123
00:10:08,447 --> 00:10:11,674
What are you all doing? Everyone, out!

124
00:10:40,306 --> 00:10:42,266
[Director Removal Request and Approval Form]

125
00:10:42,266 --> 00:10:43,550
[1. Project Information]

126
00:10:43,550 --> 00:10:44,919
[2. Reason for
Requesting the Director's Removal]

127
00:10:55,426 --> 00:10:58,797
This is my second time here,
and I still came empty-handed.

128
00:10:58,797 --> 00:11:02,175
Funny how I only remember
after I've already sat down.

129
00:11:02,175 --> 00:11:04,527
I wasn't expecting anything.

130
00:11:05,404 --> 00:11:07,766
You've got quite the attitude.

131
00:11:11,588 --> 00:11:13,739
Cut me some slack.

132
00:11:13,739 --> 00:11:17,010
Money's the only way I know
how to repay someone.

133
00:11:17,010 --> 00:11:18,023
Why are you here?

134
00:11:18,023 --> 00:11:21,862
As I said, money's the only thing
I know how to give.

135
00:11:23,690 --> 00:11:25,094
Go back to the set.

136
00:11:25,094 --> 00:11:26,966
I'll step down.

137
00:11:28,146 --> 00:11:28,856
Pardon?

138
00:11:28,856 --> 00:11:32,476
Director Ju and the crew came by today
and gave me an ultimatum.

139
00:11:32,476 --> 00:11:34,558
They said they wouldn't film without you.

140
00:11:34,558 --> 00:11:38,323
Jeez, all this just to keep one director?

141
00:11:38,323 --> 00:11:41,795
They're unbelievably reckless.

142
00:11:42,536 --> 00:11:46,558
So I've decided I'll be the one to leave.

143
00:11:48,601 --> 00:11:52,466
You really think that's a good reason?

144
00:11:52,466 --> 00:11:54,715
Why wouldn't it be?

145
00:11:54,715 --> 00:11:57,133
One look was enough to tell me everything.

146
00:11:57,133 --> 00:12:00,481
If I'm gone, this project will stay on track.

147
00:12:00,481 --> 00:12:03,409
It'll get its happy ending.

148
00:12:03,409 --> 00:12:05,268
For Ha Na...

149
00:12:06,247 --> 00:12:07,930
and for you too.

150
00:12:09,730 --> 00:12:11,484
Don't worry about the investors.

151
00:12:11,484 --> 00:12:13,914
They'll be thrilled.

152
00:12:13,914 --> 00:12:18,872
I'll keep every deal I made intact
and simply give up my position.

153
00:12:23,705 --> 00:12:28,124
Then, that's going to cost you quite a bit.

154
00:12:28,124 --> 00:12:30,178
I've gained more than enough.

155
00:12:35,838 --> 00:12:40,009
So consider this my contribution.

156
00:12:40,009 --> 00:12:42,158
Just make an incredible movie.

157
00:12:43,087 --> 00:12:44,978
Thank you,

158
00:12:45,950 --> 00:12:47,647
CEO An.

159
00:12:59,706 --> 00:13:01,529
Soo Bin,

160
00:13:04,851 --> 00:13:07,323
go make that happy ending...

161
00:13:09,373 --> 00:13:12,482
you've been dreaming of.

162
00:13:13,669 --> 00:13:14,993
Yes.

163
00:13:47,202 --> 00:13:49,000
Woo Soo Bin!

164
00:14:00,382 --> 00:14:01,675
Shall we go?

165
00:14:01,675 --> 00:14:06,030
[Jaejae Noodles]

166
00:14:06,030 --> 00:14:07,884
They're so happy together.

167
00:14:22,487 --> 00:14:25,323
This tastes even better today.

168
00:14:25,323 --> 00:14:28,836
Oh, well... I just wanted to look presentable.

169
00:14:28,836 --> 00:14:31,504
It's been a while since I've seen the crew.

170
00:14:32,246 --> 00:14:33,505
What are you talking about?

171
00:14:33,505 --> 00:14:37,130
- I said the gimbap tastes good.
- Oh...

172
00:14:38,708 --> 00:14:40,010
You said, "tastes good?"

173
00:14:40,010 --> 00:14:42,200
Though you do look good, too.

174
00:14:42,200 --> 00:14:44,482
You're dazzling me!

175
00:14:44,482 --> 00:14:46,220
Why is your skin glowing like that?

176
00:14:46,220 --> 00:14:49,556
Maybe we should just give
the Lighting Director the day off.

177
00:14:49,556 --> 00:14:50,974
Thank you.

178
00:14:50,974 --> 00:14:54,543
What? I was kidding.
Why are you taking it so seriously?

179
00:14:54,543 --> 00:14:58,531
I mean, thank you for helping me
get back on set.

180
00:14:58,531 --> 00:15:00,139
I love you.

181
00:15:00,806 --> 00:15:04,117
Who says "I love you"
in the middle of eating gimbap?

182
00:15:04,117 --> 00:15:06,323
Now, every time you eat gimbap,
I want you to think of me,

183
00:15:06,323 --> 00:15:08,408
not Geum Seong Moo.

184
00:15:08,408 --> 00:15:10,911
You're still jealous?

185
00:15:10,911 --> 00:15:12,370
That's adorable.

186
00:15:12,370 --> 00:15:14,572
You're cuter, Ju Yi Jae.

187
00:15:14,572 --> 00:15:16,707
Excuse me...

188
00:15:16,707 --> 00:15:18,674
How long have you been standing there?

189
00:15:18,674 --> 00:15:20,546
Sorry. That must've been awkward to listen to.

190
00:15:20,546 --> 00:15:21,672
Not at all.

191
00:15:21,672 --> 00:15:23,674
Your order of 100 rolls of gimbap is ready.

192
00:15:23,674 --> 00:15:25,652
Enjoy your meal!

193
00:15:28,887 --> 00:15:31,444
- Hello.
- Hello!

194
00:15:34,016 --> 00:15:35,997
Director Woo!

195
00:15:38,181 --> 00:15:41,124
[Romance Allowed on Set]

196
00:15:41,124 --> 00:15:43,360
- Hello.
- Hello!

197
00:15:43,360 --> 00:15:45,981
- Hello!
- Director Woo! Hello.

198
00:15:45,981 --> 00:15:47,886
- Hello.
- Hello.

199
00:15:47,886 --> 00:15:48,907
- Hello.
- Hello.

200
00:15:48,907 --> 00:15:50,123
- Hello.
- Oh, Director!

201
00:15:50,123 --> 00:15:51,690
- Hello.
- You're here!

202
00:15:51,690 --> 00:15:53,495
Hello!

203
00:15:53,495 --> 00:15:56,769
- Oh, Directors!
- Hello!

204
00:15:56,769 --> 00:16:00,085
Director Woo, it's so good to have you back!

205
00:16:00,085 --> 00:16:03,286
Director! Director!

206
00:16:04,285 --> 00:16:07,654
We're marking Nan Young's landing spot.
Could you check the position?

207
00:16:07,654 --> 00:16:08,708
Which scene was it again?

208
00:16:08,708 --> 00:16:11,812
We already shot the stunt for that scene.
Today we're just getting the close-up,

209
00:16:11,812 --> 00:16:14,378
- so around the same spot is fine.
- That's what I thought!

210
00:16:14,378 --> 00:16:20,438
But the stunt coordinator keeps telling me
to get your approval.

211
00:16:20,438 --> 00:16:23,203
Looks like you two have gotten pretty close.

212
00:16:23,203 --> 00:16:25,711
We're practically like old comrades now.
Right, Director Ju?

213
00:16:25,711 --> 00:16:28,643
Absolutely! Have you eaten yet?
We've got gimbap.

214
00:16:28,643 --> 00:16:30,274
I bought the gimbap, by the way.

215
00:16:30,274 --> 00:16:35,286
Everyone! Director Woo bought us gimbap!
Let's eat!

216
00:16:35,286 --> 00:16:38,142
Director Woo!

217
00:16:38,142 --> 00:16:41,392
It's been a while... Am I the gimbap now?

218
00:16:41,392 --> 00:16:42,544
Can I have three rolls?

219
00:16:42,544 --> 00:16:44,645
I bought plenty. Help yourselves.

220
00:16:44,645 --> 00:16:48,675
- The gimbap can talk now, huh?
- Welcome back!

221
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:51,929
- Please have some before you continue.
- Let's eat!

222
00:17:18,928 --> 00:17:20,533
Cut!

223
00:17:28,041 --> 00:17:30,042
- Okay!
- Okay!

224
00:17:35,895 --> 00:17:40,404
And that's a wrap on "Gyeongseong Love Song!"
Thank you, everyone!

225
00:17:40,404 --> 00:17:42,413
- Thank you all for your hard work!
- Thank you!

226
00:17:42,413 --> 00:17:44,762
Great job, everyone!

227
00:17:48,026 --> 00:17:50,156
Good job.

228
00:18:33,105 --> 00:18:36,386
Wow, the Assistant Director
really went all out tonight.

229
00:18:36,386 --> 00:18:39,119
I told you to secretly
pour some of those drinks out.

230
00:18:39,119 --> 00:18:42,119
Come on. It's a day worth celebrating.

231
00:18:42,119 --> 00:18:43,936
That's it.

232
00:18:44,944 --> 00:18:46,821
Get on my back.

233
00:18:46,821 --> 00:18:48,471
Really?

234
00:18:54,203 --> 00:18:56,782
You didn't even hesitate.

235
00:18:56,782 --> 00:18:58,545
Oh, this feels nice.

236
00:18:58,545 --> 00:19:02,476
Your broad back... I missed this.

237
00:19:02,476 --> 00:19:04,274
Has it really been 15 years?

238
00:19:04,274 --> 00:19:06,359
- I don't think so.
- Huh?

239
00:19:06,359 --> 00:19:10,341
The night you got drunk
and crashed at the hotel.

240
00:19:10,341 --> 00:19:13,205
- You carried me that night?
- Yeah.

241
00:19:13,205 --> 00:19:15,591
That's embarrassing.

242
00:19:16,176 --> 00:19:19,078
You told me to step on
your back to get ahead...

243
00:19:19,078 --> 00:19:21,952
but you actually offered me yours, huh?

244
00:19:23,368 --> 00:19:26,177
- Woo Soo Bin.
- Yeah?

245
00:19:26,177 --> 00:19:29,586
You said everyone gets nervous
before the first day of filming.

246
00:19:29,586 --> 00:19:32,364
What about after it's over?

247
00:19:32,364 --> 00:19:34,633
Is it always this scary?

248
00:19:34,633 --> 00:19:37,469
Why? Are you scared?

249
00:19:37,469 --> 00:19:42,183
With "Gyeongseong Love Song,"
I had the script... and I had you by my side.

250
00:19:42,183 --> 00:19:44,683
That's how I made it this far.

251
00:19:44,683 --> 00:19:47,695
I don't know if I'll get another chance.

252
00:19:47,695 --> 00:19:51,385
Or if whatever comes next will be any good.

253
00:19:51,385 --> 00:19:54,403
Why would you think that?

254
00:19:54,403 --> 00:19:58,072
The best is still ahead of us.

255
00:19:59,026 --> 00:20:02,133
Will you keep making films with me?
Just like we always have?

256
00:20:02,133 --> 00:20:04,832
- Of course.
- Why?

257
00:20:04,832 --> 00:20:06,745
Why wouldn't it be?

258
00:20:06,745 --> 00:20:08,712
You did just fine on your own.

259
00:20:08,712 --> 00:20:12,044
You've won awards.
You've earned everyone's respect.

260
00:20:12,044 --> 00:20:14,991
- You don't need me anymore...
- You know

261
00:20:15,632 --> 00:20:18,439
you're the reason I got into filmmaking.

262
00:20:20,639 --> 00:20:22,250
We're almost there.

263
00:20:22,843 --> 00:20:24,889
- We're here.
- Yeah.

264
00:20:32,606 --> 00:20:34,325
Yi Jae,

265
00:20:34,325 --> 00:20:37,301
it took us a long time to get here.

266
00:20:38,404 --> 00:20:43,649
Now, all we have to do is
keep walking together, hand in hand.

267
00:20:47,332 --> 00:20:50,584
Yeah... okay.

268
00:20:50,584 --> 00:20:52,713
Thanks for bringing me home.

269
00:20:52,713 --> 00:20:55,156
- You should head home too.
- Yeah.

270
00:20:55,156 --> 00:20:56,686
I'll get going.

271
00:20:58,128 --> 00:21:00,805
Want to call before we go to bed?

272
00:21:00,805 --> 00:21:03,005
I'm kind of tired, though.

273
00:21:03,722 --> 00:21:05,676
Okay.

274
00:21:05,676 --> 00:21:07,197
Good night.

275
00:21:07,197 --> 00:21:08,931
Sweet dreams...

276
00:21:09,536 --> 00:21:11,182
No, dream about me.

277
00:21:11,182 --> 00:21:12,602
Yeah.

278
00:21:12,602 --> 00:21:14,150
I'll get going!

279
00:21:42,468 --> 00:21:48,497
Actually... forget the dreams.
Just get some good sleep tonight.

280
00:21:49,433 --> 00:21:51,028
Okay?

281
00:21:51,685 --> 00:21:53,138
Good night.

282
00:21:53,759 --> 00:21:55,287
See you tomorrow.

283
00:21:56,454 --> 00:21:58,254
I'm really leaving.

284
00:22:18,012 --> 00:22:22,373
Back then, nothing scared me.

285
00:22:37,225 --> 00:22:39,400
[Original Director: Woo Soo Bin]

286
00:22:39,400 --> 00:22:41,083
[What Do I Dream Of, and Who Do I Die For?]
[The Classroom of Lost Dreams]

287
00:22:41,083 --> 00:22:44,149
[The Classroom of Lost Dreams:
The Empty Seats of Those Who Once Dreamed]

288
00:22:44,149 --> 00:22:46,659
[School of Zombie]
[A Flower Blooming on the Cliff]

289
00:22:48,284 --> 00:22:49,870
Is Yi Jae here?

290
00:22:49,870 --> 00:22:51,800
Good grief, it reeks of booze in here!

291
00:22:51,800 --> 00:22:57,285
Oh my goodness, what is all this? What a mess.

292
00:22:57,285 --> 00:23:00,172
Come on. You could've at least cleaned this up.

293
00:23:00,172 --> 00:23:01,792
Wake up!

294
00:23:02,430 --> 00:23:04,507
Oh my gosh! What is this...

295
00:23:06,552 --> 00:23:10,826
What on earth is he doing? Jeez...

296
00:23:25,053 --> 00:23:27,705
Ugh, my head hurts.

297
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:33,762
Get up, girl.

298
00:23:35,213 --> 00:23:39,470
- Get up. Get up!
- It hurts! It hurts! Oh, come on!

299
00:23:43,173 --> 00:23:47,244
Oh, you only had the broth.
I'll bring you some more.

300
00:23:49,847 --> 00:23:51,178
I feel awful...

301
00:23:51,178 --> 00:23:54,733
Nobody forced you to drink.
You did that to yourself.

302
00:23:54,733 --> 00:23:58,748
- It's not my body. It's my heart.
- Why?

303
00:23:58,748 --> 00:24:00,565
Mom.

304
00:24:00,565 --> 00:24:03,941
I watched my high school films again
for the first time in years.

305
00:24:03,941 --> 00:24:06,528
I was embarrassed the whole time.

306
00:24:06,528 --> 00:24:08,480
Why did I shoot it like that?

307
00:24:08,480 --> 00:24:10,531
I was all style and no substance.

308
00:24:10,531 --> 00:24:13,455
I guess I was fearless
because I didn't know any better.

309
00:24:14,071 --> 00:24:16,121
But you know...

310
00:24:16,121 --> 00:24:21,086
Now, I know just enough,
and maybe that's why I'm scared.

311
00:24:21,086 --> 00:24:24,414
Oh, my. You were just a clueless kid
running around with a camera.

312
00:24:24,414 --> 00:24:26,702
It's funny hearing you say that now.

313
00:24:29,541 --> 00:24:31,208
Mom.

314
00:24:32,204 --> 00:24:36,215
If I stop halfway, I won't get anywhere, right?

315
00:24:36,215 --> 00:24:39,058
I'll just be someone
who got lucky and made one good movie.

316
00:24:39,058 --> 00:24:40,968
Then I guess I raised you wrong.

317
00:24:40,968 --> 00:24:43,915
Why are you even thinking about stopping?

318
00:24:43,915 --> 00:24:46,588
Is that because I raised you that way?

319
00:24:46,588 --> 00:24:49,561
Is this because I was always
telling you not to do things?

320
00:24:49,561 --> 00:24:53,251
- No, Mom, that's not what I meant...
- Then what is it?

321
00:24:53,251 --> 00:24:57,024
Quit beating around the bush
and tell me the truth!

322
00:25:01,919 --> 00:25:03,944
I don't want to settle here.

323
00:25:03,944 --> 00:25:05,464
I want to learn more.

324
00:25:05,464 --> 00:25:09,932
I know exactly how much I still lack.
I can't just pretend I don't.

325
00:25:09,932 --> 00:25:13,388
Then there's your answer. Go learn.

326
00:25:13,388 --> 00:25:15,547
Whether it's because of me, or Young Jae,

327
00:25:15,547 --> 00:25:17,017
or because of Soo Bin...

328
00:25:17,017 --> 00:25:19,362
don't ever stop because of someone else.

329
00:25:19,362 --> 00:25:22,461
Go wherever your heart tells you to go.

330
00:25:24,336 --> 00:25:26,170
Mom...

331
00:25:27,517 --> 00:25:30,371
I should at least fry you an egg.

332
00:26:34,853 --> 00:26:37,306
Not yet...

333
00:26:37,306 --> 00:26:39,036
I'm sorry, sir.

334
00:26:41,391 --> 00:26:44,205
Where could she possibly go?

335
00:26:44,205 --> 00:26:47,722
If she's not at her parents' place,
then she has to be somewhere around here.

336
00:26:47,722 --> 00:26:50,715
She hasn't even contacted Soo Bin...

337
00:26:50,715 --> 00:26:55,233
Sir, maybe it's time to report her missing.

338
00:27:00,550 --> 00:27:02,027
What did you say?

339
00:27:02,027 --> 00:27:03,221
I'm sorry.

340
00:27:03,221 --> 00:27:09,047
I'm already a laughingstock
at the hospital and everywhere else!

341
00:27:09,047 --> 00:27:10,824
And what?

342
00:27:10,824 --> 00:27:13,482
You want me to report
my own wife missing right now?

343
00:27:13,482 --> 00:27:17,882
You want the whole town talking about me?

344
00:27:40,927 --> 00:27:45,845
That's right! I knew it.

345
00:27:45,845 --> 00:27:48,659
Where would you even go?

346
00:27:48,659 --> 00:27:50,337
You belong here!

347
00:27:50,337 --> 00:27:53,108
You always come back!

348
00:27:56,019 --> 00:27:58,230
Let's get divorced.

349
00:28:01,776 --> 00:28:04,718
- What?
- I'm asking for a divorce.

350
00:28:11,508 --> 00:28:14,370
"Divorce Registration Form..."

351
00:28:14,370 --> 00:28:19,281
Let's have lunch together,
just the two of us, for a change.

352
00:28:19,281 --> 00:28:20,638
- Mr. Kim.
- Yes, sir.

353
00:28:20,638 --> 00:28:23,042
- Book us a table.
- Yes, sir.

354
00:28:23,042 --> 00:28:26,179
Why did you even bother
getting a driver's license?

355
00:28:26,179 --> 00:28:29,501
It's not like you'd ever need to drive.

356
00:28:29,501 --> 00:28:32,295
So I could get away from you.

357
00:28:32,295 --> 00:28:36,717
Who filled your head
with these ridiculous ideas?

358
00:28:36,717 --> 00:28:41,278
Hwa Yeon,
how could you possibly live without me?

359
00:28:43,399 --> 00:28:46,939
You're the one who can't live without me.

360
00:28:46,939 --> 00:28:50,858
I was gone for a few days,
and look what it's done to you.

361
00:28:52,191 --> 00:28:54,393
- What?
- I'm the one...

362
00:28:54,393 --> 00:28:59,686
who made you look human all these years.

363
00:28:59,686 --> 00:29:04,051
From now on, live as your true self without me.

364
00:29:04,051 --> 00:29:08,251
And I'll finally live as myself, without you.

365
00:29:12,020 --> 00:29:17,381
Looks like we'll be having lunch
at home after all.

366
00:29:17,381 --> 00:29:18,908
Get over here.

367
00:29:18,908 --> 00:29:20,844
Get over here!

368
00:29:20,844 --> 00:29:22,504
Get over here!

369
00:29:22,504 --> 00:29:24,782
You little punk...

370
00:29:32,856 --> 00:29:36,485
You've... completely lost your mind, huh?

371
00:29:36,485 --> 00:29:39,976
I'm done letting you walk all over me.

372
00:29:39,976 --> 00:29:41,989
If you don't let me go,

373
00:29:41,989 --> 00:29:46,667
I'll show the whole world
what kind of monster you really are.

374
00:29:46,667 --> 00:29:50,190
I've got more than enough evidence.

375
00:29:50,190 --> 00:29:55,669
So for your own sake,
you'd better settle this quickly.

376
00:29:55,669 --> 00:29:57,496
After all,

377
00:29:58,150 --> 00:30:01,260
your reputation means more to you
than your own life, right?

378
00:30:27,661 --> 00:30:30,789
We'll have the first rough cut by then,

379
00:30:30,789 --> 00:30:33,333
so let's reschedule the meeting
with the Music Director.

380
00:30:33,333 --> 00:30:36,013
Did you listen to all the demos he sent?

381
00:30:37,087 --> 00:30:40,235
Oh, yeah. I really liked the main theme.

382
00:30:40,235 --> 00:30:42,948
It fits Nan Young and Moo Gyeom perfectly.

383
00:30:45,381 --> 00:30:49,387
What's on your mind? You seem distracted today.

384
00:30:49,387 --> 00:30:51,099
Oh, sorry...

385
00:30:51,099 --> 00:30:53,627
When's the meeting
with the Music Director again?

386
00:30:55,797 --> 00:30:58,251
How much of that did you miss?

387
00:31:02,404 --> 00:31:05,931
I was too much after we wrapped, wasn't I?

388
00:31:05,931 --> 00:31:10,968
It's not urgent.
We can go over it when the meeting's set.

389
00:31:10,968 --> 00:31:13,031
Why don't you just take it easy today?

390
00:31:14,418 --> 00:31:16,121
Soo Bin...

391
00:31:18,017 --> 00:31:20,834
- You know, I...
- Yeah.

392
00:31:20,834 --> 00:31:22,285
Well...

393
00:31:40,108 --> 00:31:41,762
Hello?

394
00:31:43,257 --> 00:31:44,795
Mom?

395
00:31:49,826 --> 00:31:52,287
Soo Bin!

396
00:31:52,287 --> 00:31:55,040
I'm getting a divorce!

397
00:31:57,918 --> 00:32:01,828
I just handed your father the divorce papers!

398
00:32:02,464 --> 00:32:04,795
I did the right thing, didn't I?

399
00:32:14,591 --> 00:32:16,895
You've been through so much, Mom.

400
00:32:16,895 --> 00:32:19,211
You really did the right thing.

401
00:32:21,598 --> 00:32:23,534
Can I...

402
00:32:24,422 --> 00:32:29,229
still be your mom, Soo Bin?

403
00:32:30,200 --> 00:32:33,314
Mom, don't say that.

404
00:32:33,314 --> 00:32:36,240
I'll always be your son.

405
00:33:01,083 --> 00:33:03,552
[Film Study Abroad Support Program]

406
00:33:06,097 --> 00:33:10,028
- Oh, you're back?
- Yeah.

407
00:33:10,028 --> 00:33:12,078
Why are you sitting here in the dark?

408
00:33:12,078 --> 00:33:15,078
- Have you had dinner?
- Not yet.

409
00:33:15,078 --> 00:33:17,744
You skipped dinner? What were you doing?

410
00:33:18,982 --> 00:33:21,521
What do you feel like eating?
I'll make it for you.

411
00:33:24,289 --> 00:33:25,881
What should I make?

412
00:33:25,881 --> 00:33:27,648
Woo Soo Bin.

413
00:33:30,287 --> 00:33:32,330
Should I study abroad?

414
00:33:33,037 --> 00:33:33,765
Why?

415
00:33:33,765 --> 00:33:38,240
Well... I've never really studied
filmmaking properly.

416
00:33:39,690 --> 00:33:43,607
I think learning on set
is just as valuable as film school.

417
00:33:43,607 --> 00:33:46,340
You can even learn faster that way.

418
00:33:46,340 --> 00:33:49,517
Then maybe I should start
paying tuition to work on set.

419
00:33:49,517 --> 00:33:51,841
Maybe we should start charging you.

420
00:33:51,841 --> 00:33:53,200
You didn't notice, did you?

421
00:33:53,200 --> 00:33:56,772
The crew always explained things to me
in way more detail.

422
00:33:56,772 --> 00:34:01,673
Things they'd explain in a few words
took me several sentences.

423
00:34:01,673 --> 00:34:04,390
I know they meant well,

424
00:34:04,390 --> 00:34:07,879
but it still made me feel so small.

425
00:34:07,879 --> 00:34:11,134
Maybe that's what
an inferiority complex feels like.

426
00:34:11,134 --> 00:34:12,851
Are you serious?

427
00:34:16,250 --> 00:34:17,891
I can't keep this from you anymore.

428
00:34:17,891 --> 00:34:20,450
I wasn't going to show you this
until editing was done, but...

429
00:34:20,450 --> 00:34:22,262
Hang on a second.

430
00:34:32,722 --> 00:34:34,317
This is it.

431
00:34:34,317 --> 00:34:36,830
Our next film.

432
00:34:39,436 --> 00:34:41,871
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]
I wrote it while I was in the States.

433
00:34:41,871 --> 00:34:44,689
You'll recognize the story once you read it.

434
00:34:45,310 --> 00:34:48,826
What? Don't tell me it's about us.

435
00:34:48,826 --> 00:34:51,884
- It is.
- That's a little...

436
00:34:51,884 --> 00:34:55,153
It's about completing
an unfinished first love through a film.

437
00:34:55,153 --> 00:34:57,264
Sounds cinematic enough, doesn't it?

438
00:34:57,264 --> 00:34:59,421
Let's polish this up and make it together.

439
00:34:59,421 --> 00:35:03,290
I'm sure it'll become even better
once you put your touch on it.

440
00:35:04,751 --> 00:35:06,797
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

441
00:35:09,720 --> 00:35:12,112
Is there a sequel by any chance?

442
00:35:12,112 --> 00:35:15,135
Why? Do you not like it because it's our story?

443
00:35:15,135 --> 00:35:16,697
No, I was just wondering...

444
00:35:16,697 --> 00:35:20,055
how far into your future plans I fit.

445
00:35:20,809 --> 00:35:23,031
I'm not saying we have to make this one.

446
00:35:23,031 --> 00:35:25,111
We can do a different story if you want.

447
00:35:25,111 --> 00:35:27,040
By your side?

448
00:35:30,769 --> 00:35:32,849
I'll have dinner at home.

449
00:35:32,849 --> 00:35:34,789
You should get some rest too.

450
00:35:46,563 --> 00:35:48,021
Yi Jae!

451
00:35:48,021 --> 00:35:50,234
I'll read it when I get home.

452
00:35:57,814 --> 00:36:01,798
But if I read it and don't think it works,
no hard feelings?

453
00:36:02,409 --> 00:36:04,582
Seriously, no mercy.

454
00:36:05,288 --> 00:36:06,905
Deal.

455
00:36:06,905 --> 00:36:08,523
I'm heading out!

456
00:36:23,848 --> 00:36:26,165
[Dream]

457
00:36:44,661 --> 00:36:46,702
[2026 Bunam International Cinema Residency]
[Open Call for Participating Directors]

458
00:36:46,702 --> 00:36:48,100
[1. Project Objectives]
[2. Recruitment Overview]

459
00:36:52,842 --> 00:36:58,095
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

460
00:37:03,707 --> 00:37:08,685
Since it's south-facing,
it gets amazing sunlight.

461
00:37:08,685 --> 00:37:11,835
The view is so beautiful, isn't it?

462
00:37:18,892 --> 00:37:20,901
Oh, my!

463
00:37:20,901 --> 00:37:24,578
Your husband is so meticulous.
And he's quite handsome too!

464
00:37:24,578 --> 00:37:26,079
Excuse me? Oh, he's...

465
00:37:26,079 --> 00:37:32,280
Honey. Won't that room be too small
with our bed and wardrobe in?

466
00:37:32,280 --> 00:37:33,740
Huh?

467
00:37:34,461 --> 00:37:37,570
Landlords usually prefer newlyweds.

468
00:37:37,570 --> 00:37:39,551
Landlord?

469
00:37:39,551 --> 00:37:42,880
If I'm buying it, wouldn't I be the landlord?

470
00:37:43,563 --> 00:37:45,138
Goodness!

471
00:37:45,138 --> 00:37:50,590
I knew you two were successful,
but I guess the wife's the real breadwinner!

472
00:37:51,399 --> 00:37:56,081
That's how I landed such a handsome husband.

473
00:37:56,081 --> 00:38:00,053
- I just showed up with myself.
- Oh, my.

474
00:38:05,778 --> 00:38:09,713
You really... enjoy your fried chicken.

475
00:38:09,713 --> 00:38:13,566
Filming's over. Do you know
how long I've been holding back?

476
00:38:14,460 --> 00:38:19,422
So, here's the thing...
Filming's over, and we kissed.

477
00:38:19,422 --> 00:38:21,841
What are we going to do now?

478
00:38:23,428 --> 00:38:25,100
I'm asking what you're going to do.

479
00:38:25,100 --> 00:38:28,392
How long are you going to
keep calling me "ma'am?"

480
00:38:28,392 --> 00:38:31,228
Here's your cheese balls!

481
00:38:31,228 --> 00:38:33,078
We didn't order these.

482
00:38:33,078 --> 00:38:36,510
Are you a celebrity by any chance?

483
00:38:36,510 --> 00:38:39,576
I'd love to get your autograph.

484
00:38:41,196 --> 00:38:43,421
How did you know?

485
00:38:44,049 --> 00:38:46,535
I tried to keep a low profile,
but I guess I can't help it.

486
00:38:46,535 --> 00:38:48,754
See? I told you!

487
00:38:48,754 --> 00:38:53,493
Please give me your autograph.
You're so handsome!

488
00:38:53,493 --> 00:38:55,650
- Me?
- Yeah.

489
00:38:57,754 --> 00:38:59,821
I'm not really famous.

490
00:38:59,821 --> 00:39:05,445
You're an actor, right?
You'll be famous soon. I'm sure of it!

491
00:39:06,261 --> 00:39:07,827
What's your name?

492
00:39:07,827 --> 00:39:10,049
Please just write "To Lee Soo Min."

493
00:39:10,049 --> 00:39:13,437
[To Lee Soo Min, Sim Yu Geon]
I'll put it up where everyone can see it!

494
00:39:13,437 --> 00:39:16,273
I guess I'll have to start
disguising him from now on.

495
00:39:16,273 --> 00:39:18,920
- Thank you.
- Yeah.

496
00:39:18,920 --> 00:39:21,604
Then the person you're with is...

497
00:39:22,613 --> 00:39:24,989
She's my girlfriend.

498
00:39:25,866 --> 00:39:29,469
Oh, I see!

499
00:39:29,469 --> 00:39:33,409
I'll be rooting for you, Mr. Sim Yu Geon!

500
00:39:33,409 --> 00:39:35,842
Your girlfriend's beautiful too!

501
00:39:37,834 --> 00:39:39,370
Alright.

502
00:39:40,477 --> 00:39:42,332
Save me...

503
00:39:46,323 --> 00:39:48,636
You're a grown man, for crying out loud!

504
00:39:48,636 --> 00:39:52,679
Boss, fish eyes freak me out!

505
00:39:59,230 --> 00:40:01,759
There. It's done, right?

506
00:40:01,759 --> 00:40:03,316
Now grab the knife.

507
00:40:03,316 --> 00:40:05,025
Boss...

508
00:40:05,025 --> 00:40:07,893
Putting me in the kitchen is bad for business.

509
00:40:07,893 --> 00:40:13,328
You're the taste of SimSim Fisheries,
and I'm the visual appeal.

510
00:40:13,328 --> 00:40:15,371
Great food and great looks! Isn't that perfect?

511
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:19,060
Even if you drowned,
that mouth of yours would still be floating.

512
00:40:19,060 --> 00:40:20,738
Are you planning to
carry plates your whole life?

513
00:40:20,738 --> 00:40:24,914
Yes. I'd be happy living like this forever.

514
00:40:24,914 --> 00:40:28,801
Going to the fish market with you,
chatting with the ladies there,

515
00:40:28,801 --> 00:40:32,935
eating good food with Mom,
and teasing my sister...

516
00:40:32,935 --> 00:40:35,989
That's what happiness is, isn't it?

517
00:40:37,929 --> 00:40:39,512
Yeah...

518
00:40:40,172 --> 00:40:42,919
That's exactly why I'm teaching you.

519
00:40:44,785 --> 00:40:47,388
Watch carefully.

520
00:40:47,388 --> 00:40:49,908
First, you cut through the spine.

521
00:40:49,908 --> 00:40:54,182
Then take everything out from inside
and cut off all the fins...

522
00:40:57,124 --> 00:41:00,650
- Cut them off, then remove the tail.
- Boss...

523
00:41:04,898 --> 00:41:09,569
Can you just... be honest with me now?

524
00:41:09,569 --> 00:41:11,540
I saw everything.

525
00:41:12,167 --> 00:41:15,913
You barely eat these days,
but you keep taking handfuls of pills.

526
00:41:16,977 --> 00:41:18,599
What are...

527
00:41:19,648 --> 00:41:21,594
those pills?

528
00:41:21,594 --> 00:41:23,093
Please tell me.

529
00:41:32,780 --> 00:41:35,505
[Topline Entertainment]

530
00:41:49,058 --> 00:41:50,852
Yeah, Young Jae.

531
00:41:51,929 --> 00:41:54,204
[SimSim Fisheries]

532
00:41:54,204 --> 00:41:56,171
Yu Geon...

533
00:41:58,140 --> 00:42:01,316
What? What happened?

534
00:42:02,397 --> 00:42:04,116
<i>Boss...</i>

535
00:42:04,116 --> 00:42:06,860
<i>No... Mr. Sim...</i>

536
00:42:06,860 --> 00:42:09,080
<i>I mean...</i>

537
00:42:09,784 --> 00:42:12,824
Your dad has cancer.

538
00:42:14,618 --> 00:42:17,285
<i>Pancreatic cancer...</i>

539
00:42:33,377 --> 00:42:36,844
Ju Young Jae! I'm coming over right now.

540
00:42:38,922 --> 00:42:41,421
I said I'm coming right now!

541
00:42:42,938 --> 00:42:45,163
Sim Yu Geon!

542
00:42:45,163 --> 00:42:46,993
Thank you...

543
00:42:47,600 --> 00:42:48,875
Where are you going?

544
00:42:48,875 --> 00:42:52,561
I'm sorry, CEO An. I'll come back another time.

545
00:42:52,561 --> 00:42:55,488
You're in no condition to ride.

546
00:42:56,743 --> 00:42:59,838
Mr. Park, give him a ride.

547
00:42:59,838 --> 00:43:01,559
Yes, ma'am.

548
00:43:12,918 --> 00:43:15,537
Why didn't you tell me?

549
00:43:18,822 --> 00:43:21,527
What would've changed if you kept hiding it?

550
00:43:21,527 --> 00:43:25,169
If you're gone, how am I supposed to live?

551
00:43:25,169 --> 00:43:28,896
Did you really have to make me
into an unfilial son?

552
00:43:28,896 --> 00:43:31,122
How are you an unfilial son?

553
00:43:31,122 --> 00:43:32,337
I was thinking about you...

554
00:43:32,337 --> 00:43:36,165
If you were thinking about me,
you should've told me!

555
00:43:36,165 --> 00:43:39,247
I'm your only family!

556
00:43:39,909 --> 00:43:41,907
You should've told me!

557
00:43:41,907 --> 00:43:45,882
Then I could've taken you to the hospital,
gotten you admitted,

558
00:43:45,882 --> 00:43:48,786
started chemo... done something!

559
00:43:48,786 --> 00:43:53,136
That's exactly why I didn't tell you, okay?

560
00:43:56,300 --> 00:43:59,930
You finally got your chance
to shine as the lead!

561
00:43:59,930 --> 00:44:02,679
How could I ask you
to throw that away and take care of me?

562
00:44:02,679 --> 00:44:05,287
An unfilial son? Fine!

563
00:44:05,287 --> 00:44:09,011
Be a bad son, then!

564
00:44:09,011 --> 00:44:13,513
I'd rather have that than be the father
who holds his son back until the very end!

565
00:44:14,209 --> 00:44:15,825
I...

566
00:44:16,571 --> 00:44:18,908
I don't want to die like that!

567
00:44:18,908 --> 00:44:22,076
I won't die like that!

568
00:44:22,076 --> 00:44:25,515
You never came when I begged you to.

569
00:44:26,625 --> 00:44:30,057
Now that I wish you wouldn't,
here you are making such a fuss.

570
00:44:36,927 --> 00:44:38,981
Yu Geon, you...

571
00:44:40,842 --> 00:44:43,380
don't come back here anymore, okay?

572
00:44:43,380 --> 00:44:48,140
After I'm gone, don't set foot here again.

573
00:44:48,140 --> 00:44:51,315
Live the rest of your life in Seoul. Okay?

574
00:44:52,234 --> 00:44:54,005
That's...

575
00:44:58,775 --> 00:45:00,780
That's your father's wish.

576
00:45:23,601 --> 00:45:25,649
They said he only has three months...

577
00:45:25,649 --> 00:45:29,804
Three months from now,
my dad might not be here anymore.

578
00:45:33,115 --> 00:45:35,080
How does that even make sense?

579
00:45:37,583 --> 00:45:40,654
I've never even imagined that...

580
00:45:41,740 --> 00:45:43,958
I regret everything.

581
00:45:45,567 --> 00:45:49,689
I should've come home when he asked.

582
00:45:49,689 --> 00:45:53,514
Maybe I would've noticed sooner.

583
00:45:54,120 --> 00:45:57,928
I was so busy chasing my dreams...

584
00:45:57,928 --> 00:46:00,301
I didn't even know my dad was sick...

585
00:46:01,011 --> 00:46:05,854
Yu Geon, don't think that way.

586
00:46:10,486 --> 00:46:12,009
Yi Jae.

587
00:46:12,812 --> 00:46:15,103
When does our movie come out?

588
00:46:15,103 --> 00:46:17,570
It won't be within three months, right?

589
00:46:17,570 --> 00:46:19,905
Can't we release it sooner?

590
00:46:19,905 --> 00:46:21,497
Soo Bin,

591
00:46:23,450 --> 00:46:25,369
please...

592
00:46:25,369 --> 00:46:27,788
I want him to see it

593
00:46:28,786 --> 00:46:30,987
before he's gone.

594
00:46:32,151 --> 00:46:35,172
I want him to see his son
filling the whole screen,

595
00:46:35,172 --> 00:46:40,061
not just someone hidden in the background.

596
00:46:46,715 --> 00:46:48,298
I'm sorry...

597
00:46:49,351 --> 00:46:51,505
I shouldn't be like this.

598
00:46:52,938 --> 00:46:54,899
I'm sorry, Soo Bin.

599
00:46:59,900 --> 00:47:03,413
We can't move up the release,

600
00:47:03,413 --> 00:47:05,805
but he can still watch the movie.

601
00:47:07,297 --> 00:47:09,233
Right, Woo Soo Bin?

602
00:47:11,970 --> 00:47:15,523
It's only a rough cut,
so it'll be a little rough.

603
00:47:15,523 --> 00:47:17,768
There won't be any music yet.

604
00:47:18,377 --> 00:47:22,787
But you'll be there...
filling the whole screen.

605
00:47:28,098 --> 00:47:29,872
Thank you.

606
00:47:45,949 --> 00:47:52,508
"Celebrating actor Sim Yu Geon,
Son of Sim Shin, on his first leading role..."

607
00:47:52,508 --> 00:47:54,604
Oh dear, that's a hard word.

608
00:47:54,604 --> 00:47:57,137
"Bu", "Debut."

609
00:47:57,137 --> 00:48:00,377
"He takes his first step as a leading actor.

610
00:48:00,377 --> 00:48:02,213
Please join us."

611
00:48:02,213 --> 00:48:04,129
Applause!

612
00:48:04,129 --> 00:48:06,187
Grandma, you're the best! Awesome!

613
00:48:06,187 --> 00:48:07,447
You'll come, right?

614
00:48:07,447 --> 00:48:09,056
I should go.

615
00:48:09,056 --> 00:48:10,876
I heard about Mr. Sim.

616
00:48:10,876 --> 00:48:14,101
How dare he leave before this old woman!

617
00:48:14,101 --> 00:48:17,767
I'm gonna give him a piece of my mind!

618
00:48:20,850 --> 00:48:23,529
["Gyeongseong Love Song" Special Screening]
Life can be so cruel...

619
00:48:23,529 --> 00:48:25,984
I'm already tearing up.

620
00:48:25,984 --> 00:48:28,269
Poor Yu Geon's father...

621
00:48:28,269 --> 00:48:31,161
Mom, don't start crying already...

622
00:48:31,161 --> 00:48:34,715
You're gonna make me cry too. Don't.

623
00:48:34,715 --> 00:48:37,142
Is Young Jae still in his room?

624
00:48:37,142 --> 00:48:39,753
Don't even ask. He's been crying nonstop.

625
00:48:39,753 --> 00:48:42,491
I should buy him some fried chicken today.

626
00:48:42,491 --> 00:48:47,364
Oh, right! I'll grab the camcorder too.
Wait a sec!

627
00:48:57,728 --> 00:49:01,258
- Have you eaten?
- Yes, I have.

628
00:49:03,713 --> 00:49:07,319
I know I left it here somewhere...

629
00:49:07,319 --> 00:49:09,882
Jeez.

630
00:49:09,882 --> 00:49:12,049
Where is it?

631
00:49:14,862 --> 00:49:16,492
What is it?

632
00:49:18,561 --> 00:49:19,626
Hello?

633
00:49:19,626 --> 00:49:23,172
<i>- Hello, is this Director Ju Yi Jae?</i>
- Yes, who is this?

634
00:49:23,172 --> 00:49:26,609
<i>This is Kim Hyun Ji
from the Bunam City Cultural Affairs Office.</i>

635
00:49:26,609 --> 00:49:30,553
<i>You recently inquired
about our residency program, correct?</i>

636
00:49:30,553 --> 00:49:32,415
Oh, yes...

637
00:49:32,415 --> 00:49:34,337
<i>I looked into your inquiry,</i>

638
00:49:34,337 --> 00:49:38,139
<i>and you mentioned that
your film is still awaiting release.</i>

639
00:49:38,139 --> 00:49:39,244
Yes.

640
00:49:39,244 --> 00:49:40,500
<i>Even in that case,</i>

641
00:49:40,500 --> 00:49:44,693
<i>you can still apply with the unfinished version
that is currently being edited.</i>

642
00:49:44,693 --> 00:49:47,988
<i>But there are a few additional documents
you'll need to submit.</i>

643
00:49:47,988 --> 00:49:52,226
<i>- Can you take some notes?</i>
- Yes... One second, please!

644
00:49:54,556 --> 00:49:57,262
<i>Ready?</i>

645
00:49:57,262 --> 00:49:58,606
[Dream, Written by Woo Soo Bin]

646
00:49:58,606 --> 00:50:01,605
Yes, go ahead.

647
00:50:02,544 --> 00:50:05,762
A director verification form,

648
00:50:05,762 --> 00:50:09,384
screening consent form... Okay.

649
00:50:09,384 --> 00:50:11,431
The production company's seal...

650
00:50:11,431 --> 00:50:14,320
and a recommendation letter? Okay.

651
00:50:14,320 --> 00:50:17,720
Thank you! Alright.

652
00:50:24,613 --> 00:50:26,480
You startled me.

653
00:50:37,996 --> 00:50:41,239
I wasn't trying to hide it...

654
00:50:41,239 --> 00:50:43,797
I haven't even applied yet.

655
00:50:44,878 --> 00:50:47,948
I guess you really didn't like my script.

656
00:50:48,610 --> 00:50:53,011
It's not that... I haven't read it yet.

657
00:50:53,011 --> 00:50:58,147
Because if I do... I feel like
I'll never want to let go of your hand.

658
00:51:00,811 --> 00:51:02,646
And what's wrong with that?

659
00:51:03,732 --> 00:51:05,533
Yi Jae.

660
00:51:05,533 --> 00:51:10,266
You're scared, right? Stay with me. It's okay.

661
00:51:11,025 --> 00:51:12,618
Yeah.

662
00:51:12,618 --> 00:51:14,643
I wouldn't be afraid with you.

663
00:51:14,643 --> 00:51:17,074
I could always lean on you.

664
00:51:18,245 --> 00:51:20,152
But...

665
00:51:21,412 --> 00:51:23,542
would I be okay like that?

666
00:51:24,209 --> 00:51:26,272
Would you?

667
00:51:26,272 --> 00:51:29,053
Why wouldn't we be?

668
00:51:29,848 --> 00:51:32,381
I don't even understand why you're doing this.

669
00:51:32,381 --> 00:51:35,979
You! It's because of you!

670
00:51:35,979 --> 00:51:38,913
If I stay by your side, I'll stop growing.

671
00:51:38,913 --> 00:51:41,830
That's why I have to leave!

672
00:51:41,830 --> 00:51:45,597
But I love you, and I don't want to lose you.

673
00:51:45,597 --> 00:51:47,521
That's why it's driving me crazy!

674
00:51:47,521 --> 00:51:50,705
Why would you stop? I'm not stopping.

675
00:51:50,705 --> 00:51:54,605
- No, that's not what I mean. I just...
- Don't go.

676
00:51:54,605 --> 00:51:57,117
I don't want to be apart from you.

677
00:51:59,283 --> 00:52:00,815
You're...

678
00:52:01,672 --> 00:52:04,916
You're so selfish.

679
00:52:04,916 --> 00:52:08,985
I can struggle with this,
but you can't ask this of me.

680
00:52:08,985 --> 00:52:12,093
You were gone for over ten years,

681
00:52:12,093 --> 00:52:15,442
and now you're telling me
I don't get to make my own choice?

682
00:52:16,801 --> 00:52:19,511
I'm asking you to choose me.

683
00:52:20,912 --> 00:52:23,632
You're more important to me
than any movie I'll ever make.

684
00:52:25,082 --> 00:52:28,066
My dream isn't filmmaking anymore.

685
00:52:28,066 --> 00:52:30,055
It's you, Ju Yi Jae.

686
00:52:33,169 --> 00:52:36,568
Don't go, Yi Jae. Please.

687
00:53:11,540 --> 00:53:13,236
Why are you taking that?

688
00:53:13,236 --> 00:53:17,600
- Just leave it. I'm throwing it away.
- It's perfectly fine. Why throw it away?

689
00:53:17,600 --> 00:53:20,788
Did you pack everything? Ready to go?

690
00:53:22,009 --> 00:53:23,889
Yeah...

691
00:53:23,889 --> 00:53:25,745
I guess so.

692
00:53:26,540 --> 00:53:28,205
Dad.

693
00:53:29,980 --> 00:53:32,721
You've worked hard.

694
00:53:33,630 --> 00:53:39,238
It's time to put the knife down
and pick up the guitar.

695
00:53:57,985 --> 00:54:00,892
[Invitation to "Gyeongseong Love Song"
Special Screening]

696
00:54:02,990 --> 00:54:05,287
For ten years, I only had one hour.

697
00:54:05,287 --> 00:54:08,243
Now I get two full hours onscreen.

698
00:54:09,467 --> 00:54:10,959
Yeah?

699
00:54:11,618 --> 00:54:14,068
It's the day after tomorrow.
So, I'll get to see your movie.

700
00:54:17,296 --> 00:54:19,298
[Celebrating actor Sim Yu Geon,
Son of Sim Shin, on his first leading role]

701
00:54:19,298 --> 00:54:20,344
[Please join us]

702
00:54:28,521 --> 00:54:30,799
Oh, but what do I do?

703
00:54:31,480 --> 00:54:33,515
I have a date that day.

704
00:54:35,247 --> 00:54:38,306
I think it'd be okay if you came with her.

705
00:54:38,306 --> 00:54:40,307
Can you handle it?

706
00:54:42,407 --> 00:54:44,793
[Closed Today]

707
00:54:44,793 --> 00:54:47,246
Actor Sim Yu Geon...

708
00:54:47,246 --> 00:54:50,181
First leading role... Wow, that's amazing.

709
00:54:50,181 --> 00:54:52,114
[Thanks to all of you,
SimSim Fisheries was never a boring place]

710
00:54:52,114 --> 00:54:53,126
You did great.

711
00:54:53,126 --> 00:54:55,775
[We sincerely thank you for your support
and will be taking a short break]

712
00:55:06,706 --> 00:55:09,013
Yeah, yeah. Hello!

713
00:55:09,013 --> 00:55:11,796
[Actor Sim Yu Geon's First Leading Role,
"Gyeongseong Love Song" Special Screening]

714
00:55:27,413 --> 00:55:29,303
Yi Jae!

715
00:55:30,744 --> 00:55:32,645
You're here!

716
00:55:32,645 --> 00:55:34,352
- We're here!
- We're here!

717
00:55:34,352 --> 00:55:36,880
You've worked hard.

718
00:55:45,690 --> 00:55:47,615
- Come here.
- Come here!

719
00:55:47,615 --> 00:55:50,346
Look at you, you've gotten so pretty.
My goodness.

720
00:55:50,346 --> 00:55:52,936
- Go say hi to Uncle Soo Bin.
- Say hello.

721
00:55:52,936 --> 00:55:55,310
Hello.

722
00:55:55,310 --> 00:55:57,649
Hello! How have you been?

723
00:55:57,649 --> 00:56:00,068
Oh, good job. Come here, Seong Chan.

724
00:56:00,068 --> 00:56:03,812
- Come here.
- Step aside, there's a car coming.

725
00:56:04,740 --> 00:56:06,604
Whose car is this?

726
00:56:06,604 --> 00:56:10,334
Director! I'm here too!

727
00:56:12,164 --> 00:56:14,741
Ms. Oh Ha Na! I'm a huge fan!

728
00:56:14,741 --> 00:56:17,639
That looks heavy. Let me carry it!

729
00:56:17,639 --> 00:56:18,788
- Who is he...
- He's...

730
00:56:18,788 --> 00:56:24,263
I'm Director Ju Yi Jae's
one and only younger brother, Ju Young Jae.

731
00:56:24,263 --> 00:56:26,011
Oh, nice to meet you.

732
00:56:26,011 --> 00:56:29,469
- Then I'll take you up on that.
- Yeah, sure...

733
00:56:29,469 --> 00:56:33,477
- By the way, where's Yu Geon?
- He's inside the hall. Go on.

734
00:56:33,477 --> 00:56:35,261
Well...

735
00:56:35,261 --> 00:56:36,994
Not even a hello for me.

736
00:56:36,994 --> 00:56:40,814
They really must be close.
Nicely done, Sim Yu Geon.

737
00:56:41,985 --> 00:56:43,726
Jeez...

738
00:56:47,568 --> 00:56:49,678
Yu Geon!

739
00:56:50,410 --> 00:56:52,259
Ha Na!

740
00:56:53,736 --> 00:56:56,176
What are you doing here?

741
00:56:58,293 --> 00:57:01,558
Today, you can lean on my shoulder.

742
00:57:05,480 --> 00:57:09,524
Why'd you make me buy a suit...

743
00:57:09,524 --> 00:57:11,869
Oh my gosh! What should I do?

744
00:57:11,869 --> 00:57:14,552
Hello, sir!

745
00:57:14,552 --> 00:57:16,180
Yes...

746
00:57:18,866 --> 00:57:22,092
Aren't you the actress
starring with my Yu Geon?

747
00:57:22,092 --> 00:57:23,789
Yes.

748
00:57:23,789 --> 00:57:27,182
But what were you two doing...

749
00:57:27,182 --> 00:57:31,201
Oh, it's... it's a pleasure to meet you.

750
00:57:31,201 --> 00:57:34,899
I'm Oh Ha Na, Yu Geon's girlfriend.

751
00:57:34,899 --> 00:57:36,994
I see.

752
00:57:39,289 --> 00:57:41,272
Excuse me?

753
00:57:41,272 --> 00:57:44,403
Yeah, she's my girlfriend.

754
00:57:45,382 --> 00:57:49,338
Girl... girlfriend?

755
00:57:51,997 --> 00:57:56,802
Now that's my son! What a good son!

756
00:57:56,802 --> 00:57:59,256
He's been quite popular with girls.

757
00:58:01,100 --> 00:58:03,694
[Gyeongseong Love Song]

758
00:58:03,694 --> 00:58:06,048
- It's starting!
- It's starting!

759
00:58:08,580 --> 00:58:11,700
[Oh Ha Na]

760
00:58:11,700 --> 00:58:12,807
[Sim Yu Geon]

761
00:58:12,807 --> 00:58:14,979
That's my handsome buddy!

762
00:58:14,979 --> 00:58:19,087
Come on, my friend Sim Yu Geon! Let's go!

763
00:58:22,125 --> 00:58:23,869
<i>What do you think?</i>

764
00:58:23,869 --> 00:58:28,280
<i>Not under Wolhajeong's lights,
but here under the moonlight.</i>

765
00:58:28,280 --> 00:58:33,102
<i>I'm not sure. From every angle,
you seem free of all worries.</i>

766
00:58:33,102 --> 00:58:37,362
<i>From every angle... Truly beautiful.</i>

767
00:58:37,362 --> 00:58:41,345
<i>I mean myself, reflected in your eyes.</i>

768
00:58:43,897 --> 00:58:47,406
<i>How are you always joking?</i>

769
00:58:48,885 --> 00:58:55,222
<i>We each live our lives
making a movie of our own.</i>

770
00:59:02,403 --> 00:59:05,482
<i>Just as every film has its defining scene,</i>

771
00:59:08,891 --> 00:59:11,030
<i>every life...</i>

772
00:59:11,681 --> 00:59:13,929
<i>has one too.</i>

773
00:59:13,929 --> 00:59:17,783
<i>- I don't think I've seen you before.
- My name is Nan Young.</i>

774
00:59:20,408 --> 00:59:22,506
I can see it all.

775
00:59:35,342 --> 00:59:39,489
<i>If I couldn't protect you,
how could I ever protect the country?</i>

776
00:59:59,346 --> 01:00:01,392
[This film is dedicated to Sim Shin,
father of actor Sim Yu Geon]

777
01:00:06,773 --> 01:00:13,211
<i>A defining scene is built
from countless moments.</i>

778
01:00:13,211 --> 01:00:16,831
[This film is dedicated to Sim Shin,
father of actor Sim Yu Geon]

779
01:00:42,103 --> 01:00:45,512
I may not even make it to 60,

780
01:00:46,232 --> 01:00:49,441
but you've given me a moment I'll never forget.

781
01:00:49,441 --> 01:00:51,284
Thank you.

782
01:00:53,694 --> 01:00:58,867
Seeing my son achieve his dream
so wonderfully today reminds me of...

783
01:00:58,867 --> 01:01:01,523
my own dream when I was young.

784
01:01:01,523 --> 01:01:04,206
I have no regrets leaving,

785
01:01:04,206 --> 01:01:07,936
but I'd like one proud memory to hold onto.

786
01:01:07,936 --> 01:01:10,280
Would you allow me to play something for you?

787
01:01:10,280 --> 01:01:13,317
- Nice!
- Sounds good!

788
01:01:23,698 --> 01:01:25,549
You did well.

789
01:02:39,942 --> 01:02:42,567
<i>I know exactly...</i>

790
01:02:43,183 --> 01:02:47,280
<i>what scene I have to write next.</i>

791
01:02:53,986 --> 01:02:57,488
<i>Don't go, Yi Jae. Please...</i>

792
01:03:04,522 --> 01:03:06,172
<i>Soo Bin...</i>

793
01:03:08,371 --> 01:03:10,797
<i>I love you...</i>

794
01:03:12,042 --> 01:03:14,763
<i>but you are not my dream.</i>

795
01:03:14,763 --> 01:03:17,508
<i>I already chose you once,</i>

796
01:03:17,508 --> 01:03:22,220
<i>and that choice haunted me for a long time.</i>

797
01:03:24,592 --> 01:03:27,304
<i>This time, I'm staying on the bus.</i>

798
01:03:28,503 --> 01:03:30,653
<i>This time, instead of you...</i>

799
01:03:31,552 --> 01:03:33,962
<i>I'm choosing my dream.</i>

800
01:04:25,357 --> 01:04:30,752
<i>I decided to let go of Woo Soo Bin's hand.</i>

801
01:04:32,493 --> 01:04:35,106
<i>So I can create my own defining scene.</i>

802
01:05:19,143 --> 01:05:21,160
<i>I'm not going to love you anymore!</i>

803
01:05:21,160 --> 01:05:23,317
<i>Why are you making me say something like this?</i>

804
01:05:23,317 --> 01:05:26,519
<i>Say your final goodbye, and let it go now.</i>

805
01:05:26,519 --> 01:05:29,179
<i>- Choi Sa Rang?
- Oh my, where did everyone go?</i>

806
01:05:29,179 --> 01:05:31,442
<i>- What was that again?
- It's Dad playing the guitar.</i>

807
01:05:31,442 --> 01:05:32,266
<i>Ju Yi Jae!</i>

808
01:05:32,266 --> 01:05:36,496
<i>I hope this doesn't keep you from moving on,
but gives you the strength to endure.</i>

809
01:05:36,496 --> 01:05:38,313
<i>Thanks to you, I found my dream again.</i>

810
01:05:38,313 --> 01:05:40,387
<i>I'll make something incredible
out of it over the next two years.</i>

811
01:05:40,387 --> 01:05:43,327
<i>I told you it's not too late,
and you should go see Yi Jae.</i>

812
01:05:43,327 --> 01:05:46,830
<i>I guess... I still haven't gotten over you.</i>
